Attacks adds a graph to Reporting, Health: packets blocked coming in on each
WAN interface, per minute, as two lines. One counts every blocked packet; the
other counts those blocked by rules whose source is a blocklist, such as
Spamhaus DROP loaded into a URL Table alias.

It adds no settings and no page of its own; an Attacks dashboard widget shows
the last 24 hours. A WAN is any enabled interface with a gateway
or an address obtained from the provider (DHCP, PPPoE and the like). A
blocklist rule is an enabled block or reject rule, inbound, on that interface,
whose source is an alias filled from a URL (URL, URL Table or URL Table JSON).
Health keeps the history: per minute for 20 hours, then coarser for up to 6
years.

